# MathViz Visual Audit

## Issues Found

### 1. 🔴 Duplicate Math Formula in Sidebar
The right sidebar shows the same math formula **twice** when a step has a `math` property:
- Once inside the `StepNarrative` component (with copy button)
- Again in a separate `KaTeXBlock` card below it

````carousel
![Step 1 showing duplicate f(x) = x² - 2x - 3](/Users/oli/.gemini/antigravity/brain/eb1d08a8-3c2e-4581-b86a-4defb17a1290/initial_visualizer_state_1775745765321.png)
<!-- slide -->
```diff
- {currentStepData?.math && (
-   <div className="rounded-lg bg-white/[0.03] border border-white/[0.06] px-4 py-3">
-     <KaTeXBlock latex={currentStepData.math} color="rgba(255,255,255,0.85)" />
-   </div>
- )}
```
The StepNarrative already renders the math — the separate KaTeXBlock is redundant.
````

### 2. 🟡 TOC Panel Overlaps Scene Tabs
The Table of Contents panel (`top-12 left-3`) visually overlaps the scene tabs row behind it, creating confusion.

![TOC overlapping scene tabs](/Users/oli/.gemini/antigravity/brain/eb1d08a8-3c2e-4581-b86a-4defb17a1290/toc_panel_visible_1775745817860.png)

### 3. 🟡 Header/Controls Hidden Initially  
On lesson load, the header toolbar and playback controls auto-hide due to a 4-second idle timer, but since the user just loaded, they may still be orienting. The step dots and scene tabs also lack a visible progress/playback bar.

### 4. ✅ Elements Verified Working
- Welcome screen: centered, clean, no overlaps
- Canvas rendering: parabola, points, labels all render correctly
- Lesson picker: clean modal with search, tabs, favorites
- Keyboard shortcuts overlay: well-organized 2-column grid
- Responsive layout (800x600): sidebar moves to bottom correctly
- Label collision avoidance on canvas is working (vertex, y-int, root labels don't fully overlap)

## Fixes Applied

| Issue | Fix |
|-------|-----|
| Duplicate math formula | Removed redundant KaTeXBlock below StepNarrative |
| TOC panel overlap | Adjusted top offset from `top-12` to `top-28` to clear all header bars |

